; Real-terminal scenarios: the built TUI inside tmux, panes captured and
; compared by cram (dune promote re-records). Each .t file is a group of
; scenarios from harness.sh; dune runs the groups in parallel. Skipped when
; tmux is absent. They run the backend too, from the other dune project:
; ../e2e/backend.digest (its hash) runs them again when it changes, and only
; then. The default run has only smoke.t; the other groups are in the slow
; tier (PRIGH_TEST_TIER=full, ./test --full). A new group goes in the list
; below.

(cram
 (deps harness.sh %{bin:prigh-tui} ../e2e/backend.digest)
 (enabled_if %{bin-available:tmux}))

(cram
 (applies_to approvals basics connection signin terminal tools)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{env:PRIGH_TEST_TIER=default} full)))
